            "bullet_text": "Allulose (D-Psicose) is a rare sugar that occurs naturally in small quantities in figs, raisins, and kiwi fruit. It is classified as a monosaccharide with the same molecular formula as fructose but a different molecular arrangement — this structural difference is why it tastes like sugar but is not metabolised as sugar."
